From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XeresRazor <shinohara@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:43:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] shader_split: read Fenrir's gzip streams of BNSH files
 (Valkyria Chronicles 4)

Valkyria Chronicles 4's shaders are gzip streams of BNSH files, every stream with
the same ten header bytes (1f8b08 00 00000000 00 0b): 6,712 in the HSPK package
FENRIR_SHADER_NEW_NX64_.HSG (a CRI CPK entry) and 158 in main (its built-in
fen_prim_* shaders). No reader decompressed them, so the split found 0 shaders
and the build stopped with "the shader split found no shaders in main or the
RomFS".

gzip_bnsh_shaders takes a stream only with that exact header, complete and with
BNSH inside, and bounds the decoded bytes of all of them to NEST times the
file's. scan_blob calls it for an HSPK file, main() for each version's main.
Each BNSH holds one stage, so the shaders are single-stage programs.

The split gives 6,870 keys (RomFS 6,712, main 158), identical to the 6,870
programs the game creates in its first 60 seconds (a temporary host change dumped
the image behind every nvnProgramSetShaders). 16 other games' main have no stream
with that header, so their tables do not change. A Mac build passes all steps and
the game reaches its opening scenes and first map screen at about 30 fps.

test_gzip_bnsh.py builds synthetic packages (no game files). The format and the
check are in docs/reference/shaders.md and docs/agents/01-extract.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Valkyria Chronicles 4's shaders are gzip streams of BNSH files that no shader_split reader decompressed: the split found 0 shaders and the build stopped
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1279

