+### Gzip streams of BNSH files in a Fenrir package and in main
+
+- **Symptom:** `[RED] the shader split found no shaders in main or the RomFS` on a RomFS of four CRI CPKs (`FEN_0000.CPK`, 10.7 GB, 27,458 files) and a `main` with no shader container, no GLSLC output and no control-section magic. The game imports `glslcCompile` and never calls it (its GLSLC imports are unbound).
+- **How it is stored:** two places, both gzip streams of one BNSH file each, every stream with the same ten header bytes `1f 8b 08 00 00 00 00 00 00 0b` (no flags, no time, OS 11). 6,712 are in `FENRIR_SHADER_NEW_NX64_.HSG` (17 MB, stored in the CPK), a package that starts `HSPK` (then a `KSPK` table of 135 programs by name and hash, `EOFC`, a `KSPP` package and its relocation tables). 158 more, the built-in `fen_prim_*` shaders (58 names in `main`), lie in `main`'s data as 4 KB-aligned arrays. Each BNSH holds one stage: 3,435 vertex and 3,435 pixel shaders in all, at most 4,259 bytes stored and 10,512 decoded.
+- **Why nothing found them:** the BNSH are inside compressed streams, so the scan for BNSH, GLSLC and control-section magics saw none. Where the game decodes them: its start-up inflates them with the SDK's zlib (`nnutilZlib_inflate`, window bits 31) into 4 KB-aligned buffers, then `main+0x59b28c` checks the `BNSH` magic and hands them to `nn::gfx` (`ShaderImpl::Initialize`, `main+0x64c640`, which calls `nvnProgramSetShaders` six stages at a time).
+- **Fix:** `shader_split.py` `gzip_bnsh_shaders` takes a stream only with that exact header, complete and with `BNSH` inside, and bounds the decoded bytes of all of them to `NEST` times the file's. `scan_blob` calls it for an `HSPK` file, `main()` for each version's main. The shaders are single-stage programs (`SINGLE_STAGE`, `#GZ@`). `dm/tools/tests/test_gzip_bnsh.py` has synthetic packages.
+- **Checked:** the split gives 6,870 keys (RomFS 6,712, main 158), **identical to the 6,870 programs the game creates in its first 60 seconds** (a temporary host change dumped the image behind every `nvnProgramSetShaders`), including the 33 it draws with at its start. 16 other games' `main` (Breath of the Wild, Metroid Dread, Mina the Hollower, Advance Wars 1+2 among them) have no stream with that header, so their tables do not change.
+- **Not checked:** the translation of the 6,870 shaders and a run of the game with them. The check boots with no shader libraries.
